<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    A LaunchAgent for the morning brief. macOS only; see docs/scheduling.md.

    The companion to com.stonksmith.nightly.plist, which scrapes at 18:30. This
    one reads what that wrote and opens it at 06:30, and the two are separate
    agents because they answer to different clocks: a scrape has to run after the
    close, and a reminder has to run when somebody is awake to read it.

    Two values below have to be edited, and they are the same two the nightly
    agent needs. There is no way for a committed file to know either.

      ProgramArguments   the absolute path to scripts/stonksmith-morning.sh in
                         your checkout. The script finds the repository from its
                         own location, so this is the only path to set.

      PATH               must contain uv. `which uv` says where yours is; uv's
                         installer puts it in ~/.local/bin, which is not in the
                         list below, and launchd does no tilde expansion here.

    Install, from the repository:

        mkdir -p ~/Library/LaunchAgents
        sed "s|/PATH/TO/StonkSmith|$PWD|; s|^\(.*<string>\)/usr/local/bin|\1$(dirname "$(command -v uv)"):/usr/local/bin|" \
            scripts/com.stonksmith.morning.plist > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.stonksmith.morning.plist
        launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.stonksmith.morning.plist

    `launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.stonksmith.morning` removes it, and
    `launchctl kickstart -p gui/$(id -u)/com.stonksmith.morning` runs it now
    rather than waiting for the morning, which is how to test it.

    gui/$(id -u) matters twice over here. It is what lets a LaunchAgent read the
    login keychain, which is the reason the nightly agent needs it, and this one
    additionally has to open a browser, which an agent outside the GUI session
    has no display to do. Bootstrapped into a system domain, this would write a
    brief every morning and show it to nobody.

    StartCalendarInterval fires on wake if the machine was asleep at the time,
    which cron does not. A laptop that is shut at 06:30 is the ordinary case
    rather than the exception, so this is the difference between a brief that
    appears when the lid opens and one that never appears at all.

    Nothing here re-scrapes. The brief reports on the previous evening's run, so
    a morning where it says "no new scrape" is reporting a failure of the
    nightly agent rather than of this one. Read /tmp/stonksmith-nightly.log in
    that case, not this agent's log.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.stonksmith.morning</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/sh</string>
        <string>/PATH/TO/StonkSmith/scripts/stonksmith-morning.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
    </dict>

    <!-- Weekdays, because the nightly run is weekdays: a Saturday brief would
         report a carried-forward flat line by construction. Weekday 1 is
         Monday; 0 and 7 are both Sunday. -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>1</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>2</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>3</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>4</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>5</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
    </array>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/stonksmith-morning.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/stonksmith-morning.log</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
